Base: zune-jpeg 0.5.15 as crates.io publishes it

Not applied: the tree has no fork of zune-jpeg, and whether to carry one is doc/questions/Q227.
Found by the `jpeg_bands` fuzz target (ADR 1495). `decode_dc` already updates the DC prediction
with `wrapping_add`; the dequantising multiply beside it does not, so a frame whose DC differences
accumulate past i32 range under a 16-bit quantiser panics wherever overflow checks are on (the dev,
test and fuzz profiles) and wraps in release. This makes the multiply wrap as the addition does,
which is release's behaviour in every profile. The reproduction is the 847-byte codestream below
(hexadecimal), decoded whole to RGBA:
